-# Working notes: 926c6bd137d3
+# Current decisions: 926c6bd137d3, version 3.0.0
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Rule and domain
+
+For each complete yellow (4) rectangular frame, fill its blank interior cells
+with its one interior marker's color. Preserve the marker, yellow border, and
+all exterior objects. Zero is the background. Marker colors are the eight
+nonzero, nonyellow colors; separate frames may use the same color, and exterior
+objects may use marker colors. The canonical Racket program is unchanged and
+is pinned by `RULE_HASH = '575c55ee70e4'`.
+
+The validator recognizes 1–4 disjoint, nonnested boxes, each at least 4×4,
+with complete four-connected yellow perimeters and exactly one interior
+nonzero, nonyellow cell. It accepts lawful edge placement, diagonal contact,
+and nonyellow exterior objects touching a border. It rejects broken/joined
+yellow outlines, missing/multiple markers, and nested frames. The generator
+uses a one-cell separator for constructive packing; the validator is broader.
+Construction also reserves at least one blank exterior cell. For example,
+5×5/one 4×4 frame/nine exterior cells is rejected explicitly even though a
+hand-built saturated exterior can satisfy the morphology validator.
+
+## Reversed choices and evidence
+
+The imported version 2.0.1 used placement-index colors, omitted exterior
+objects, silently dropped requested frames after retries, and checked marker
+presence globally. Its original rationale is unknown. Review
+`review-a7304ba015dd369f:v0001` recorded these on the exact selected baseline
+`ffd12ccb0525dd22e55d145a6915df0a122f87662fec78f109668aa019fa21b6`.
+This review independently reproduced 96/96 erase-exterior rival agreements,
+0/96 exterior witnesses, 16/64 four-frame shortfalls, and the moved-marker
+false acceptance. See this return's `checks/repair-regressions/` evidence and
+the small fixtures in `counterexamples/review-134d82626bc7bd77/`.
+
+Version 3.0.0 randomizes and repeats marker roles, emits preserved exterior
+cells, guarantees complete packing with a bounded fallback, and observes
+exact controls from the returned grid. It validates each frame geometrically
+and checks requested metadata. The focused tests cover the old failures,
+canonical inputs, legal boundary cases, and incompatible controls.
+
+The existing review index still says `needs_triage` and binds the old source.
+That historical status has not been rewritten. The repair addresses its three
+findings with new evidence; maintainer intake owns any resolution update.
+
+## Distribution and exact controls
+
+`grid_h` and `grid_w` accept 5–22; `n_frames` accepts 1–4;
+`palette_size` accepts 3–10 and counts **all** input colors, including 0 and 4;
+`n_distractors` accepts 0–12 and counts exterior nonzero **cells**, not objects.
+`n_distinct_colors` is a compatibility alias for the same palette control,
+not an independent axis. Conflicting aliases and impossible joint requests
+raise explicit errors with the actual incompatible override names.
+Retired inert controls are rejected. Named negative textures remain diagnostic
+fixtures outside the lawful axis domain and cannot bypass validation.
+
+Even for hard difficulty, canonical-profile draws retain the five observed
+size/palette profiles. Contrast draws vary geometry and have difficulty limits
+of 16, 19, or 22 for easy, medium, or hard. Exterior cells form both clusters
+and singletons. Rich contrasts use at least two distinct frame-marker colors
+and include a marker role outside the canonical marker-color set.
+
+Default lessons use three demonstrations and one query. The period-four
+schedule is canonical, contrast, contrast, canonical. Any consecutive
+four-draw window contains two rich contrasts, so holding out one pair still
+leaves a demonstration that refutes each of the six declared rivals. The
+claim concerns normal default lessons; arbitrary exact overrides can remove
+those witnesses and do not inherit this teaching guarantee.
+
+## Validation, remaining limits, and authority
+
+The final generator passes the twelve-stage after battery with required
+rotations and no advisories. Evidence includes a source-bound fixed-seed
+census of all four starts in every band and a larger randomized census.
+The tests enumerate 192 windows over seeds 0–15, four starts and three bands
+using an independent Python fill control; the separate censuses use Racket
+labels. These are finite checks against six declared functions, not proof
+against every possible rule or every random seed. See the return's REVIEW.md
+and RESULTS.json for final counts and exact commands.
+
+No canonical row or Racket semantics changed. The selected authority record's
+`target_code` had two extra comments; it now contains the canonical program
+text exactly. The archive's raw program was already canonical and is unchanged.
+Training admission and historical audit status are not changed by this review.
